---
import Base from "../../layouts/Base.astro";
import g from "../../data/manuscripts/gollenesse.json";

const doubts = g.entries.filter((e) => e.doubt).length;
const first = g.pages[0];
const letters = [...new Set(g.entries.map((e) => e.hw.replace(/^[^A-Za-z]+/, "").charAt(0).toUpperCase()))].filter(Boolean);
const payload = { pages: g.pages, scanUrl: g.archive.scan_url, entries: g.entries.map((e) => ({ n: e.n, page: e.page, pages: e.pages })) };
---
<Base title={`${g.title}: Malabar glossary (${g.year})`} nav="tables"
  description={`An unpublished 1743 manuscript glossary of ${g.entries.length} Malabar (Kerala) terms by the VOC commander of Cochin, J. V. Stein van Gollenesse, shown beside its page images with transcription and translation.`}>
  <article class="ms">
    <header class="wrap ms-head">
      <nav class="crumbs" aria-label="Breadcrumb"><a href="/">Tables</a><span aria-hidden="true">/</span><span>Manuscripts</span></nav>
      <div class="ms-title">
        <div>
          <h1 class="print">Mallabars woordenboek</h1>
          <p class="ms-sub">Malabar terms explained in Dutch · <span>{g.author}</span> · Cochin, {g.year}</p>
        </div>
        <dl class="ms-stats mono">
          <div><dt>Entries</dt><dd>{g.entries.length}</dd></div>
          <div><dt>Pages</dt><dd>{g.pages.length}</dd></div>
          <div><dt>Uncertain</dt><dd>{doubts}</dd></div>
        </dl>
      </div>
      <div class="prose ms-intro">
        <p>In 1743 the departing commander of the Dutch East India Company at Cochin, Julius Valentijn Stein van Gollenesse, left his successor a long memoir on the Malabar Coast. He ended it with “some notes in the form of a dictionary of the chief kingdoms, lands, towns, bazaars, pagodas, rivers, festivals and names in Malabar arranged in alphabetical order”, so that a new chief meeting an unknown word in letters and palm-leaf <i>olas</i> would not have to ask people “who might sometimes inform him wrong”.</p>
        <p>The memoir was printed at Madras in 1908 from the copy kept in India, but the glossary was not: in his 1911 translation A. Galletti marked it “[missing]”. The copy sent to the Netherlands survives in the Company's archive at The Hague. It has been cited at least once, by J. B. Mailaparambil for its entry on the Ali Rajas of Cannanore, but we have found no edition or translation. It is shown here page by page, with a transcription and an English translation.</p>
      </div>
      <p class="notice soft"><strong>Draft edition.</strong> Transcribed from the page images and checked against them once. Readings marked [?] are uncertain. The modern identifications are proposals, checked against each entry's own description (distances, neighbours, rulers) but mostly not yet against sources; each shows its confidence, and hovering shows the reasoning. Malayalam script is given only for high-confidence identifications. All of this needs review by specialists in Malayalam and Kerala history; corrections are welcome.</p>
    </header>

    <div class="wrap ms-work">
      <section class="ms-scan" aria-label="Page images">
        <div class="ms-scan-tools mono">
          <button type="button" data-prev aria-label="Previous page">←</button>
          <span data-pagelabel>Scan {first.scan}</span>
          <button type="button" data-next aria-label="Next page">→</button>
          <a data-archive href={g.archive.scan_url + first.scan} target="_blank" rel="noopener">Nationaal Archief ↗</a>
        </div>
        <img class="ms-img" data-img src={first.sm} srcset={`${first.sm} 900w, ${first.lg} 1800w`} sizes="(max-width: 1000px) 92vw, 46vw"
          width={first.w} height={first.h} alt={`Scan ${first.scan} of the manuscript`} />
      </section>

      <section class="ms-list" aria-label="Entries">
        <div class="ms-filter">
          <input type="search" placeholder="Filter: headword, Dutch, English or modern name" data-filter aria-label="Filter entries" />
          <nav class="ms-letters mono" aria-label="Jump to letter">{letters.map((l) => <a href={`#l-${l}`}>{l}</a>)}</nav>
        </div>
        <ol class="ms-entries">
          {g.entries.map((e, i) => {
            const l = e.hw.replace(/^[^A-Za-z]+/, "").charAt(0).toUpperCase();
            const prev = i ? g.entries[i - 1].hw.replace(/^[^A-Za-z]+/, "").charAt(0).toUpperCase() : "";
            return (
              <li id={`e${e.n}`} data-n={e.n} class="ms-e" data-text={`${e.hw} ${e.nl} ${e.en} ${e.id?.modern || ""}`.toLowerCase()}>
                {l !== prev && <span id={`l-${l}`} class="ms-anchor" />}
                <button type="button" class="ms-hw print" data-goto={e.n}>{e.hw}{e.doubt && <span class="ms-doubt mono" title="Contains uncertain readings">?</span>}</button>
                <p class="ms-nl">{e.nl}</p>
                <p class="ms-en">{e.en}</p>
                {e.id && (
                  <p class={`ms-id ms-id-${e.id.conf}`} title={e.id.basis}>
                    <span class="mono">{e.id.conf === "low" ? "Possibly" : "Modern"}</span>
                    {e.id.modern}{e.id.ml && <span class="ms-ml" lang="ml"> {e.id.ml}</span>}{e.id.where && <span class="ms-where"> · {e.id.where}</span>}
                    <span class="ms-conf mono">{e.id.conf}</span>
                  </p>
                )}
                <p class="ms-meta mono"><a href={`#e${e.n}`}>№ {e.n}</a>{e.folio && <span>fol. {e.folio}</span>}</p>
              </li>
            );
          })}
        </ol>
      </section>
    </div>

    <footer class="wrap prose ms-foot">
      <h2>Source and citation</h2>
      <p>{g.archive.holder}, {g.archive.ref}: “Een Mallabars woordenboek, behorende tot voorsz. Memorie”, appended to the memoir of J. V. Stein van Gollenesse for Reinicus Siersma, Cochin, 1743. The copy ends with a collation note (“Accordeert”) and signature. Page images: Nationaal Archief, via the GLOBALISE project's IIIF manifests. The glossary was found by searching the GLOBALISE machine transcriptions of the VOC archive (CC0).</p>
      <p>Printed editions of the memoir: <i>Memoir on the Malabar Coast by J. V. Stein van Gollenesse, composed in the year 1743</i>, Selections from the Records of the Madras Government, Dutch Records No. 1 (Madras, 1908); A. Galletti, A. J. van der Burg and P. Groot, <i>The Dutch in Malabar</i>, Dutch Records No. 13 (Madras, 1911), where the glossary is marked “[missing]”. Cited from the Hague copy in J. B. Mailaparambil, <i>The Ali Rajas of Cannanore, Dutch East India Company and the Kolattiris, 1663–1723</i> (PhD thesis, Leiden, 2007), p. 55 n. 122, published as <i>Lords of the Sea</i> (Brill, 2012).</p>
    </footer>
  </article>
</Base>

<script is:inline define:vars={{ D: payload }}>
  const img = document.querySelector("[data-img]");
  const label = document.querySelector("[data-pagelabel]");
  const arch = document.querySelector("[data-archive]");
  let cur = 0;
  function show(i) {
    cur = Math.max(0, Math.min(D.pages.length - 1, i));
    const p = D.pages[cur];
    img.srcset = `${p.sm} 900w, ${p.lg} 1800w`; img.src = p.sm; img.width = p.w; img.height = p.h;
    img.alt = `Scan ${p.scan} of the manuscript`;
    label.textContent = `Scan ${p.scan}`;
    arch.href = D.scanUrl + p.scan;
  }
  document.querySelector("[data-prev]").onclick = () => show(cur - 1);
  document.querySelector("[data-next]").onclick = () => show(cur + 1);
  const byN = Object.fromEntries(D.entries.map((e) => [e.n, e]));
  document.querySelectorAll("[data-goto]").forEach((b) => b.addEventListener("click", () => {
    document.querySelectorAll(".ms-e.on").forEach((x) => x.classList.remove("on"));
    b.closest(".ms-e").classList.add("on");
    show(byN[b.dataset.goto].page);
    if (matchMedia("(max-width: 1000px)").matches) img.scrollIntoView({ behavior: "smooth", block: "start" });
  }));
  const items = [...document.querySelectorAll(".ms-e")];
  document.querySelector("[data-filter]").addEventListener("input", (ev) => {
    const q = ev.target.value.trim().toLowerCase();
    for (const li of items) li.hidden = q && !li.dataset.text.includes(q);
  });
  const h = location.hash.match(/^#e(\d+)$/);
  if (h && byN[h[1]]) { show(byN[h[1]].page); document.getElementById(`e${h[1]}`)?.classList.add("on"); }
</script>

<style>
  .ms-head { padding-block: 1.5rem 1rem; }
  .ms-title { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 1rem 2rem; align-items: end; justify-content: space-between; margin-top: .5rem; }
  .ms-title h1 { margin: 0; font-size: var(--s-4); line-height: 1.1; }
  .ms-sub { color: var(--ink-2); margin: .35rem 0 0; }
  .ms-stats { display: flex; gap: 1.5rem; margin: 0; }
  .ms-stats dt { font-size: var(--s-0); color: var(--ink-3); }
  .ms-stats dd { margin: 0; font-size: var(--s-2); }
  .ms-intro { margin-top: 1.25rem; max-width: 46rem; }
  .ms-head .notice { max-width: 46rem; margin: 1rem 0 0; padding: .7rem 1rem; border: 1px solid var(--rule); border-left: 3px solid var(--accent); border-radius: var(--radius); background: var(--bg-2); color: var(--ink-2); font-size: var(--s-1); }
  .ms-head .notice strong { color: var(--ink); }
  .ms-work { display: grid; grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr) minmax(0, 1fr); gap: 2rem; align-items: start; padding-bottom: 2rem; }
  .ms-scan { position: sticky; top: 1rem; }
  .ms-scan-tools { display: flex; gap: .75rem; align-items: center; font-size: var(--s-0); margin-bottom: .5rem; color: var(--ink-2); }
  .ms-scan-tools button { border: 1px solid var(--rule); background: var(--surface); color: var(--ink); border-radius: var(--radius); padding: .2rem .6rem; cursor: pointer; }
  .ms-scan-tools a { margin-left: auto; color: var(--accent); }
  .ms-img { width: 100%; height: auto; max-height: calc(100vh - 5rem); object-fit: contain; background: var(--bg-2); border-radius: var(--radius); }
  .ms-filter { position: sticky; top: 0; background: var(--bg); padding-block: .5rem; z-index: 1; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--rule); }
  .ms-filter input { width: 100%; padding: .5rem .7rem; border: 1px solid var(--rule); border-radius: var(--radius); background: var(--surface); color: var(--ink); font: inherit; }
  .ms-letters { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: .5rem; margin-top: .5rem; font-size: var(--s-0); }
  .ms-letters a { color: var(--accent); text-decoration: none; }
  .ms-entries { list-style: none; margin: 0; padding: 0; }
  .ms-e { padding: .9rem .5rem; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--rule-2); border-radius: 4px; }
  .ms-e.on { background: var(--accent-soft); }
  .ms-anchor { display: block; position: relative; top: -7rem; }
  .ms-hw { all: unset; cursor: pointer; font-size: var(--s-3); color: var(--ink); }
  .ms-hw:hover, .ms-hw:focus-visible { color: var(--accent); text-decoration: underline; }
  .ms-doubt { font-size: var(--s-0); color: var(--ink-3); margin-left: .35rem; vertical-align: super; }
  .ms-nl { margin: .35rem 0 0; color: var(--ink); }
  .ms-en { margin: .35rem 0 0; color: var(--ink-2); }
  .ms-id { margin: .45rem 0 0; font-size: var(--s-1); color: var(--ink); }
  .ms-id > .mono:first-child { font-size: var(--s-0); color: var(--accent); margin-right: .5rem; text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: .04em; }
  .ms-id-low { color: var(--ink-2); }
  .ms-ml { color: var(--ink-2); }
  .ms-where { color: var(--ink-3); }
  .ms-conf { font-size: var(--s-0); color: var(--ink-3); margin-left: .5rem; border: 1px solid var(--rule); border-radius: 999px; padding: 0 .45rem; }
  .ms-meta { margin: .4rem 0 0; font-size: var(--s-0); color: var(--ink-3); display: flex; gap: 1rem; }
  .ms-meta a { color: inherit; }
  .ms-foot { padding-block: 1rem 3rem; max-width: 46rem; }
  @media (max-width: 1000px) {
    .ms-work { grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr); }
    .ms-scan { position: static; }
  }
</style>
